{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1244155-huntsmen-chronicle-vs-ctl2ed","id":1244155,"title":"Huntsmen Chronicle vs CtL2ed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-09T08:24:25-07:00","id":1244155,"title":"Huntsmen Chronicle vs CtL2ed","content":"Hi, I've not been following the developments closely over the last few years but I seem to recall that CtL 2ed was meant to contain an actual sample chronicle akin to the God-Machine Chronicle. I noticed the anthology is still called the &quot;Huntsmen Chronicle&quot; anthology but can't seem to find any recent references to the Huntsmen Chronicle itself. Was that plan abandoned? Or is it upcoming in some hazy future?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T08:34:04-07:00","id":1244158,"title":"","content":"Not really.<br /> <br /> The Huntsmen themselves are very much still a thing in CtL2e and receive a good amount of focus. It's just that the antagonist chapter isn't called the &quot;Huntsmen Chronicle&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T08:52:25-07:00","id":1244162,"title":"","content":"The Chronicle subtitles generally have no dedicated sections of the book. Instead the books simply have a little more focus on those. For example, the Idigam Chronicle lists a few idigam in the Werewolf antagonist chaper, but it also contains other types of antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T08:56:08-07:00","id":1244165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>genesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1244155-huntsmen-chronicle-vs-ctl2ed#post1244155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, I've not been following the developments closely over the last few years but I seem to recall that CtL 2ed was meant to contain an actual sample chronicle akin to the God-Machine Chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite.<br /> <br /> Every Second Edition gameline has had some variant of &quot;this game includes the X Chronicle&quot; as a general statement of what the game's primary means of shaking up the status quo or offering up an unusual circumstance for the PCs to look into. Before officially-termed second editions were approved, these served as the subtitle for their gamelines' updates to the Revised Storytelling System rules \u2014 Requiem 2e was Blood and Smoke: The Strix Chronicle, for instance, while Forsaken 2e was The Wolf Must Hunt: The Idigam Chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T11:52:49-07:00","id":1244235,"title":"","content":"The last game-line I followed in detail was Demon. That was already in the 2nd edition line (though before the use of that terminology) and the core book contained a sample chronicle &quot;How an Angel Dies&quot;. Sounds like the later books stopped doing that? Since SAS are no longer a thing either, are there no products for pre-fab one-shot stories or chronicles anymore? (This is obviously a general question across all lines but I am specifically interested in the new Changeling)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T12:03:22-07:00","id":1244238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>genesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1244155-huntsmen-chronicle-vs-ctl2ed?p=1244235#post1244235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last game-line I followed in detail was Demon. That was already in the 2nd edition line (though before the use of that terminology)</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon uses the Revised Storytelling System that the assorted Second Editions do, but it and Beast and Deviant are not themselves Second Editions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and the core book contained a sample chronicle &quot;How an Angel Dies&quot;. Sounds like the later books stopped doing that? </div> </div> </div>That was a thing that First Edition did. The Second Editions have generally moved to larger numbers of sample settings and scenarios in their corebooks a la Demon's Seed Collection instead of putting a single scene-by-scene premade story in a focal &quot;signature setting&quot; like Promethean, Mummy, Demon, and Beast have done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T16:50:04-07:00","id":1244315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>genesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1244155-huntsmen-chronicle-vs-ctl2ed?p=1244235#post1244235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last game-line I followed in detail was Demon. That was already in the 2nd edition line (though before the use of that terminology) and the core book contained a sample chronicle &quot;How an Angel Dies&quot;. Sounds like the later books stopped doing that? Since SAS are no longer a thing either, are there no products for pre-fab one-shot stories or chronicles anymore? (This is obviously a general question across all lines but I am specifically interested in the new Changeling)</div> </div> </div> </div>If it helps, note that the games that get Kickstarters often end up with stretch goals that produce jumpstarts, which are intro adventures that also include all the basic rules you need to get started. CtL2 will have one of those, we're working on it right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}